Description: Throw the desktop to Google Cast devices
 Throw finds the Chromecasts, Google TVs and TVs with Google Cast built in on
 the network, each as it names itself, and throws the desktop to one of them:
 the device becomes one more screen of Stereo KWin, at its own mode, with the
 3D formats and eye swap of a monitor in Display Settings, and the device plays
 that screen's picture as a live stream. A Throw page in System Settings lists
 the devices, shows what each says about itself and sets its volume; a command,
 sparky-stereo-throw, does the same from a terminal. Every failure is said and
 kept until a Throw to that device works again.
